+++ b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@ The server exposes tools across three modules in `crates/app/src/mcp/` (see `cra
 
 ### 4. Stock & Tool Management (`tools.rs`, `edit.rs`, #355)
 - `set_stock { "box"?: { "dx", "dy", "dz" }, "cylinder"?: { "diameter", "height" }, "from_model"?: string }`: Define setup stock as a box in mm (centred in XY, z from 0 to `dz`), a cylinder, or a copy of a model's mesh.
+- `set_raw_stock_only { "on": boolean }`: For a stock made from a model (`set_stock` `from_model`), say whether that source model is raw stock only - a casting or blank you cut into, not the finished part. Default off: the model is judged like every model. On: the gouge verdict leaves it out. One undo step. Refused by name when the active stock is not made from a model. The mark holds only while the model is still the stock's source and its geometry is unchanged; otherwise it is ignored and the post says so by name. An operation that machines the model (as its source or in a boundary pick) puts it back in the verdict. If the mark leaves nothing to judge, the post is refused by name.
 - `list_tool_catalog {}`: List built-in tool definitions.
 - `add_tool { "catalog"?: string, "definition"?: object, "name"?: string }`: Add a tool: a copy of a `list_tool_catalog` entry, or a full definition (`get_job`'s tool shape); `name` defaults to the catalog name.
 - `list_holder_library {}`: List the built-in holders (BT30/BT40/CAT40 with ER or Weldon, standalone ER chucks) with dimensions and the shanks each takes.

